WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:03.060
The Batman rumors and leaks just keep on coming.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.890
Let's get it out of the way from the start:
potential spoilers for the newest Batman flick

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:07.540
lay ahead.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.460
According to We Got This Covered, sources
familiar with the production are reporting

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.200
that the forthcoming film's plot will focus
on the efforts of the World's Greatest Detective

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.120
to track down a serial killer on the loose
in Gotham City.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.170
Writer/director Matt Reeves is said to be
taking his cues from the iconic Batman comic

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.090
miniseries "The Long Halloween" in crafting
his story.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:29.320
Previously, separate alleged leaks that hit
the web have indicated that the Robert Pattinson-starring

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:33.940
flick will feature no fewer than six villains,
with the Penguin and Catwoman being front

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:34.440
and center.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.299
Also said to be taking part in the villainous
goings-on: the Riddler, Two-Face, Firefly,

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.120
and the Mad Hatter.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.639
Reeves has previously stated that he'll be
going for a much different version of the

00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:48.049
Dark Knight than any we've seen on film thus
far, one which will highlight the Caped Crusader's

00:00:48.049 --> 00:00:49.600
legendary detective skills.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:53.560
It'll be a more grounded, noir-ish take on
the Batman mythos than has previously been

00:00:53.569 --> 00:00:56.569
explored in the character's multiple cinematic
incarnations.

00:00:56.569 --> 00:01:00.269
According to We Got This Covered's sources,
The Batman's plot will follow Bruce Wayne

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:04.540
as he attempts to get to the bottom of a rash
of mysterious murders plaguing Gotham City.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.490
Presumably, this investigation will take him
down multiple paths — and this is where

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.420
the flick's large assortment of iconic baddies
could come into play.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.880
The report's insiders assert that, while Penguin,
Catwoman, and the Riddler will be featured

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.980
prominently, the remaining three villains
will be relegated to comparatively minor roles.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.720
There's no word yet on whether or not all
the bad guys will be fully fledged villains,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.140
or if they'll be versions of those characters
who have yet to fully develop into themed

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:28.150
super-jerks.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:31.510
But this wouldn't be the first time a superhero
flick would have a large assortment of bad

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:34.060
guys appearing in various stages of their
career.

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:38.380
Just a couple years ago, Spider-Man: Homecoming
featured the Vulture as the main villain,

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:43.719
but also boasted appearances large and small
from Spidey bad guys like the Tinkerer, Scorpion,

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.420
the Prowler, and two Shockers.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.820
That's six villains right there, so the groundwork
for The Batman to follow a similar path to

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.520
success has already been laid at the movie
theater.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:57.479
Overall, The Batman could be laying the foundation
for a series of movies whose antagonists will

00:01:57.479 --> 00:02:01.609
have fleshed-out backstories and well-established
motivations — things which other superhero

00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:05.149
films afflicted with the dreaded Villain Bloat
have neglected to provide.

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:07.000
We're looking at you, Spider-Man 3.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:11.200
At any rate, we've previously expressed our
opinion that Reeves — a very capable filmmaker

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.849
who knows his way around a good story — knows
what he's doing in taking on the formidable

00:02:14.849 --> 00:02:16.920
task of rebooting Batman yet again.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.900
For that matter, while the internet may have
gone temporarily insane when Pattinson was

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:24.650
cast as Bruce Wayne, there's every reason
to believe that he'll absolutely crush it

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.300
in the role.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:29.920
Reeves is a highly competent director of actors,
and he knows just as well as anyone that Pattinson's

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:34.069
filmography — which has featured amazing
turns in smaller, lesser-known films such

00:02:34.069 --> 00:02:39.320
as 2017's Good Time and 2018's High Life — has
revealed him to be a much, much better actor

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.680
than fans only familiar with the Twilight
series would ever expect.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.260
At this point, we're going to go ahead and
say that if you're not excited for The Batman

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:49.049
yet, it's probably a good time to rethink
your position.

00:02:49.049 --> 00:02:54.200
The flick doesn't hit screens until June 25,
2021, and we'll be keeping close tabs on every

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.920
bit of information there is to report between
now and then.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:00.480
Keep an eye on the Batphone in case it starts
to ring…you never know when you might need

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.120
to pick up.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.340
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.360
Plus, even more Looper videos about your superhero
movies are coming soon.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:11.460
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

